# Queries & Flags System — Implementation Plan (v2)

## Background

Current system: minimal `queries` table + single [addQuery()](file:///c:/xampp/htdocs/areabazaar/core/Controllers/QueryController.php#17-43) method. All dashboards call `api/queries/add`. The [AuthController](file:///c:/xampp/htdocs/areabazaar/core/Controllers/AuthController.php#11-85) returns JSON but implements no server-side session or cookie state. The `global_settings` table (key/value store) exists and is the hook for runtime feature flags.

This plan expands the system in **6 phases**, with auth hardening as Phase 0.

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Caller Identity During Dev:** While auth sessions are built in Phase 0, every dashboard will immediately inject the current user's parameters as a PHP-injected JS variable (`window.currentUser`) during development — hardcoded per page, per role. This is replaced by session-derived values once Phase 0 is live.

> [!NOTE]
> **Notification Delivery:** In-app notifications are the default and are always active. Email and SMS notifications are wired up but **only fire** when their respective `global_settings` keys are set to `1`. Polling interval is also driven by `global_settings`, defaulting to 30 seconds.

---

## Proposed Data Schema Changes

### ALTER `queries`
```sql
ALTER TABLE `queries`
  ADD COLUMN `priority`       ENUM('Low','Normal','High','Critical') DEFAULT 'Normal',
  ADD COLUMN `status`         ENUM('Open','Closed','Archived') DEFAULT 'Open',
  ADD COLUMN `assigned_to`    INT UNSIGNED,
  ADD COLUMN `assigned_role`  VARCHAR(50),
  ADD COLUMN `closed_by`      INT UNSIGNED,
  ADD COLUMN `close_reason`   TEXT,
  ADD COLUMN `last_activity`  TIMESTAMP DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP ON UPDATE CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,
  ADD COLUMN `created_at`     TIMESTAMP DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
```

### NEW: `query_responses`
```sql
CREATE TABLE `query_responses` (
  `id`             BIGINT UNSIGNED AUTO_INCREMENT PRIMARY KEY,
  `query_id`       BIGINT UNSIGNED NOT NULL,
  `responder_id`   INT UNSIGNED NOT NULL,
  `responder_role` VARCHAR(50) NOT NULL,
  `message`        TEXT NOT NULL,
  `forwarded_to`   INT UNSIGNED,
  `forwarded_role` VARCHAR(50),
  `created_at`     TIMESTAMP DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,
  FOREIGN KEY (`query_id`) REFERENCES `queries`(`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE
) ENGINE=InnoDB;
```

### NEW: `query_response_notes`
```sql
CREATE TABLE `query_response_notes` (
  `id`          BIGINT UNSIGNED AUTO_INCREMENT PRIMARY KEY,
  `response_id` BIGINT UNSIGNED NOT NULL,
  `author_id`   INT UNSIGNED NOT NULL,
  `author_role` VARCHAR(50) NOT NULL,
  `note`        TEXT NOT NULL,
  `created_at`  TIMESTAMP DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,
  FOREIGN KEY (`response_id`) REFERENCES `query_responses`(`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE
) ENGINE=InnoDB;
```

### NEW: `query_notifications`
```sql
CREATE TABLE `query_notifications` (
  `id`             BIGINT UNSIGNED AUTO_INCREMENT PRIMARY KEY,
  `query_id`       BIGINT UNSIGNED NOT NULL,
  `recipient_id`   INT UNSIGNED NOT NULL,
  `recipient_role` VARCHAR(50) NOT NULL,
  `type`           ENUM('NewAssignment','NewResponse','PriorityChange','ThreadClosed') NOT NULL,
  `message`        TEXT,
  `is_read`        TINYINT(1) DEFAULT 0,
  `created_at`     TIMESTAMP DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,
  INDEX idx_recipient (`recipient_id`, `is_read`)
) ENGINE=InnoDB;
```

### NEW: `query_audit_log`
```sql
CREATE TABLE `query_audit_log` (
  `id`         BIGINT UNSIGNED AUTO_INCREMENT PRIMARY KEY,
  `query_id`   BIGINT UNSIGNED NOT NULL,
  `actor_id`   INT UNSIGNED NOT NULL,
  `actor_role` VARCHAR(50) NOT NULL,
  `action`     VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL,
  `detail`     TEXT,
  `created_at` TIMESTAMP DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
) ENGINE=InnoDB;
```

### `global_settings` — New Keys to Seed
```sql
INSERT IGNORE INTO global_settings (setting_key, setting_value) VALUES
  ('notif_poll_interval_seconds', '30'),
  ('notif_email_enabled',         '0'),
  ('notif_sms_enabled',           '0'),
  ('notif_email_from',            'no-reply@areabazaar.com'),
  ('notif_sms_gateway_url',       ''),
  ('notif_sms_api_key',           ''),
  ('session_lifetime_minutes',    '120'),
  ('session_secure_cookie',       '1');
```

