## Verification Plan

### API Tests (via [test_api.php](file:///c:/xampp/htdocs/areabazaar/public/test_api.php) or Postman)
1. `POST api/auth/staff-login` — valid creds → session set, cookie returned
2. `GET api/auth/check` — valid session → returns user data; expired/missing → 401
3. `POST api/auth/logout` — session destroyed, cookie expired
4. `POST api/queries/add` — record with correct creator fields
5. `GET api/queries/list` — all open threads returned
6. `POST api/queries/respond` — response + `query_notifications` row created
7. `POST api/queries/assign` — `assigned_to` updated + notification created
8. `POST api/queries/set-priority` — priority updated + notification created
9. `POST api/queries/close` — status = `Closed`
10. `GET api/queries/cold-audit` — only stale (>4 days) threads
11. `POST api/queries/prune-archive` — only closed >28 days become `Archived`
12. `POST api/queries/close-cold` — `query_audit_log` entry confirmed in DB

### Manual Browser Tests
1. Open any dashboard → notification bell renders with `0` badge
2. Submit query → appears in `admin_queries.php` as Open thread
3. Admin assigns to WHM → WHM bell updates to unread count
4. WHM responds → Admin bell updates; thread visible in Admin detail panel
5. Admin adds note to WHM's response → note visible inline in thread
6. Originating user closes own thread → status = `Closed` system-wide
7. Set `notif_email_enabled = 1` in `global_settings` → submit query → verify email log entry (or error log for dev with no mailer configured)
8. Set a test thread's `last_activity` >4 days ago in DB → Cold Audit shows it
9. Admin clicks Prune → Closed threads >28 days become `Archived`
10. Admin force-closes cold thread → `query_audit_log` entry visible in DB
